"notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental roll-forward uses fund balances (cash, investments, due from funds) from p5 as beginning/ending cash; identity 1,314,843 + 1,256,031 - 1,177,073 + 44,874 - 10,000 = 1,428,675. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4-5); business-type from Total Proprietary Funds (p7), business_type measure is net position (3,076,313 to 3,507,569; transfers net -34,874, bond proceeds 450,000). Printed 'Sales and miscellaneous taxes' 226,952 equals 'Sales taxes' on the statement of activities (p2), so categorized as sales tax. Business-type spending listed by object, categorized utilities. Proprietary cash-flow statement (p8) not recorded since basis is cash (proprietary null). Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1) total column; no liabilities printed. Detail: only budgetary comparison schedules (p9-19); no other detail schedule so no double counting. Budget schedule actuals for the budget funds Police, Fire, Library and Keno are part of 'Other Governmental Funds'; Keno has no printed total revenues line (only 5 investment earnings). Budgeted amounts are 'Original and Final' combined. Business-type fund schedule totals (water/sewer/garbage) differ from p7 only by depreciation and capital outlay presentation. Read pages 1-19 of 19"
